Worked example: a session that broadened usefully, then was reined in (twimc)

This very session (ubersitrep, 2026-08-01) is a specimen of the essay's thesis.
One "dcp" widened into: copilot-has-no-continue -> are-sessions-deterministic ->
the essay strand itself -> dispatch's quick-answer lane. Every hop was useful,
NOT a distraction. That's the trap: broadening FEELS like progress (and here it
genuinely was), but the context bill all lands in one ever-growing window. The
naive failure mode wears a productive disguise.

The non-naive move isn't "stop having ideas" — it's CAPTURE THE BRANCH AND
CLOSE IT rather than walk down it in the live window. Each branch got
discharged to its proper home instead of living on:
- determinism aside -> idea spooled to aifabric-essay
- the essay -> its own strand (parked, not drafted in-session)
- quick-answer refinement -> landed in dispatch.md, done
Then: dcp (flush to durable storage) and CLOSE the window. The session is
disposable; discharge its value, then let it go. Remaining context is spent fuel.

Twimc discipline (the CV frame): everything written in-session — spec, idea,
strand mission — is written to be legible to a reader who wasn't in the room.
The artifacts ARE the evidence, so they must speak for themselves. Reining in a
broadening session, and writing twimc as you go, are two faces of the same
sophistication: value must survive the disposal of the session that made it.

Good self-contained anecdote for the wisdom essay: shows the method being
practised on itself, in real time, including the moment of noticing the drift.
